"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nPerson Note\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nBirth<br />\n    1825<br />\n    Tennessee, USA<br />\nDeath<br />\n    unknown<br />\n    Clark County, Arkansas, USA<br />\nBurial<br />\n    Bethlehem African American Cemetery<br />\n    Joan, Clark County, Arkansas, USA<br />\nMemorial ID<br />\n    245022963 \u00b7 View Source\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nHarriet was born about 1825 in Tennessee. She married Jacob (Jake) Knox, June 10, 1866 in Clark County, Arkansas. Their known children are Isom (step son to Jacob), James (Jim), Tempe, Nathaniel, Delia, Ransom, Amiziah, Tarnetta and John Isaiah Knox.\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n1870 - Caddo, Clark County, Arkansas\n</p>\n<p>\n1900 - Caddo, Clark County, Arkansas\n</p>\n<p>\n1910 - Caddo, Clark County, Arkansas (widowed)\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nNote from Kathy Stroope Veasey, profile manager:\n</p>\n<p>\nHarriett, was enslaved in the household of Jacob Stroope, a white man ( my third great grandfather). DNA has proven that Isom (Stroope) Knox was their child. Harriett's daughter, Jane was born 1840 in Clark County, Arkansas. She married ... Mitchell. Possibility she is Jacob Stroope's biological daughter, like Harriett's oldest child, Isom. Would like to hear from anyone descended from any of Harriet's children. \n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nSpouse\n</p>\n<p>\n    Jacob \"Jake\" Knox\n</p>\n<p>\n    1819 \u2013 unknown\n</p>\n<p>\nChildren\n</p>\n<p>\n    PVT Benjamin Stroop\n</p>\n<p>\n    1843\u20131864<br />\n    Isom (Knox) Stroope\n</p>\n<p>\n    1843\u20131927<br />\n    James \"Jim\" Knox\n</p>\n<p>\n    1851\u20131914<br />\n    Jonathan Isiah \"John\" Knox\n</p>\n<p>\n    1865\u20131942\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nhttps://www.findagrave.com/memorial/245022963/harriet-knox\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
