"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nPerson Note\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nMarva Flowers Obituary<br />\nObituary published on Legacy.com by Broecker Funeral Home on Jun. 5, 2026.<br />\nIn Loving Memory of Dyann Newburn, June 27, 1952 \u2013 June 1, 2026 .\n</p>\n<p>\nDyann was a fierce, loving, nurturing, caring, and compassionate woman whose greatest gift was her ability to make everyone feel welcome. Her heart knew no limits, and her home was always open to family, friends, neighbors, and even strangers who quickly became family. She had a remarkable way of making people feel loved, supported, and valued, and her kindness touched countless lives throughout the years.\n</p>\n<p>\nAbove all else, Dyann cherished her family. She was a devoted mother to her four children: Barry Newburn (TX), Justin Newburn (AR), Jason Newburn (AR), and Joselyn Duval (Dominique)(CO). Her children were the pride and joy of her life, and she dedicated herself to ensuring they knew the depth of her love.\n</p>\n<p>\nShe was also a proud and loving grandmother to Jordan E. Tiemann (Jordan J), BJ Newburn, Jaden Newburn, and Zoe Howard, Andrey Newburn, and Allan Newburn. Nothing brought her greater happiness than spending time with her grandchildren and watching them grow. She was further blessed with five great-grandchildren, whom she adored dearly and three sisters: Bernice Seawood (TX), Mable House (AR), and Lillie Owens (AR).\n</p>\n<p>\nDyann leaves behind a host of nieces, nephews, extended family members, and friends who will forever cherish the memories they shared with her. Her warmth, generosity, strength, and unwavering love created a legacy that will continue to live on through all who knew her.\n</p>\n<p>\nShe was preceded in death by her beloved mother, Ruby Newburn; her father, Tanner Newburn; and her brothers, Jimmy Newburn and Thomas Newburn.\n</p>\n<p>\nThough our hearts are broken by her passing, we find comfort in knowing that Dyann's love, wisdom, and spirit will remain with us always. Her life was a testament to compassion, resilience, and selfless devotion to others.\n</p>\n<p>\nShe will be deeply missed and forever remembered. \"Those we love don't go away; they walk beside us every day, unseen, unheard, but always.\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nhttps://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/name/marva-flowers-obituary?id=61626142\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nPerson Note\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nM.C. Newburn Books was a beloved independent local bookstore formerly located at 950 San Pablo Avenue in Albany, California, run by Maurice Newburn. The shop regularly hosted author events and book release parties, particularly for mystery and local writers, but it has long since closed.About the Former StoreLocation: 950 San Pablo Avenue, Albany, CA 94706Owner: Maurice (M.C.) NewburnKnown For: Hosting community literary events, genre fiction, and local author readings.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
